notes['TRAINER_QUINCY']['ai'] += ' Neutralizing Gas suppresses Power Construct; Complete requires the ability active and HP at or below half, followed by a later eligible Mega decision.'
notes['TRAINER_COLTON']['disposition']='REVISE'
notes['TRAINER_COLTON']['assessment'] += ' Replace only ordinary red Floette with Eternal Flower Floette because the native Mega transition is exclusive to Eternal.'
notes['TRAINER_RONALD']['disposition']='REVISE'
notes['TRAINER_RONALD']['assessment']="Kingdra and Moxie Gyarados form the serious opening; Sash Magikarp is a constrained Flail reserve, Tentacruel controls speed and Mega Raichu Y finishes. Preserve this five-member team and change Raichu's Thunderbolt to Thunder: Mega Y has No Guard, so the move uses its actual ability for greater power and paralysis chance at a lower PP budget."
notes['TRAINER_RONALD']['ai']="Recompute Mega Raichu Y's No Guard, including reciprocal incoming accuracy; before Mega, Thunder also benefits from active rain. Magikarp's Flail requires actual current HP, Sash, weather and order, not a joke-based reserve priority."
notes['TRAINER_RONALD']['counterplay']="Electric threatens several Water members but is neutral on Kingdra. Pressure the rain/setup opening and use chip or priority against low-HP Flail. Mega Raichu Y loses Lightning Rod for No Guard: its Thunder is reliable, but opposing moves also gain the relevant accuracy benefit."
notes['TRAINER_SUSIE']['disposition']='REPAIR'
notes['TRAINER_SUSIE']['assessment']="No Guard Pidgeot pressures immediately beside Probopass's Wide Guard/paralysis. White Herb Leaf Storm enables Sceptile's Unburden, Boots protect Volcarona, Arcanine offers physical priority and Mega Froslass closes with Snow Warning. Retain Ice Beam for focused, weather-independent reliability; correct the stale claim that Mega Froslass keeps Cursed Body."
notes['TRAINER_SUSIE']['ai']="No Guard is reciprocal; White Herb consumption triggers Unburden only after an actual drop. Mega Froslass sets snow through Snow Warning and loses Cursed Body, so reserve weather and Ice defensive effects must be recomputed."
changes={
 'TRAINER_QUINCY':{'slot':5,'updates':{'species':'ZYGARDE_50_POWER_CONSTRUCT','ability':'POWER_CONSTRUCT'},'reason':'Only Zygarde Complete has the Zygardite Mega transition. Power Construct supplies the required in-battle path; Aura Break50cannot reach it. Preserve all other authored data and require a subsequent valid Mega turn after Complete activates.'},
 'TRAINER_COLTON':{'slot':5,'updates':{'species':'FLOETTE_ETERNAL'},'reason':'Floettite works only on Eternal Flower Floette; ordinary red Floette has no Mega form-change table. Use the already obtainable Eternal form and preserve every other authored field.'},
 'TRAINER_RONALD':{'slot':4,'updates':{'moves':['THUNDER','FAKE_OUT','NASTY_PLOT','PROTECT']},'reason':'Mega Raichu Y gains No Guard; Thunder uses its accuracy guarantee and opening rain rather than leaving stronger accurate Electric pressure unused. Lower PP remains a deliberate tradeoff.'},
 'TRAINER_PHOEBE':{'slot':3,'updates':{'species':'DUSCLOPS','item':'EVIOLITE','ability':'PRESSURE','nature':'CALM','points':'32/0/16/0/18/0','offset':2,'moves':['NIGHT_SHADE','WILL_O_WISP','HELPING_HAND','PAIN_SPLIT']},'reason':'Restore Phoebe\'s defining Dusclops as a durable burn, damage and partner-enabling presence. Shedinja\'s coverage-check niche is intentionally replaced; Giratina/Lunala and the remaining authored threats stay intact.'},
 'TRAINER_GLACIA':{'slot':4,'updates':{'species':'WALREIN','item':'LEFTOVERS','ability':'THICK_FAT','nature':'MODEST','points':'32/0/16/16/2/0','offset':3,'moves':['HYDRO_PUMP','BLIZZARD','ENCORE','PROTECT']},'reason':'Restore the signature Walrein with Fire/Rock matchup coverage and Encore, while preserving Veil, snow renewal, Tailwind, Chien-Pao and Mega Baxcalibur. Glastrier\'s campaign showcase is intentionally displaced; no arbitrary showcase quota forces an unrelated swap.'},
 'TRAINER_WALLACE':{'slot':5,'updates':{'nature':'JOLLY','points':'2/32/0/0/0/32','moves':['LIQUIDATION','PSYCHO_CUT','AQUA_JET','PROTECT']},'reason':'The actual Mega Starmie ability is Huge Power, unused by its all-special baseline. This physical rain finisher adds pressure through the other defensive category and priority while preserving Misty Terrain.'}
}
plans={
'TRAINER_QUINCY':"Slaking opens beside Neutralizing Gas Weezing and attacks on consecutive turns. Butterfree supports with redirection and Tailwind; Durant can transfer Truant for a later gas-free phase and Terrakion supplies attacks/Quick Guard. Power Construct Zygarde50can become Complete at the native half-HP threshold while its ability is active, then use Zygardite on a subsequent eligible turn.",
'TRAINER_COLTON':"Liepard enables Fezandipiti's Tailwind and offensive Toxic Chain pressure. Alolan Persian and Incineroar control exchanges; Mesprit supports with Helping Hand/paralysis. Eternal Flower Floette is the Mega-eligible closer, gaining Fairy Aura and using Moonblast, Calm Mind and Wish.",
'TRAINER_RONALD':"Kingdra establishes rain beside Moxie Gyarados. Magikarp is a constrained Focus Sash/Flail reserve and Tentacruel provides Icy Wind. Mega Raichu Y gains No Guard and can exploit Thunder, with Fake Out and Nasty Plot as situational options.",
'TRAINER_PHOEBE':"Giratina opens with burns and Icy Wind beside Shadow Shield Lunala's Calm Mind. Marshadow steals opposing boosts, while Eviolite Dusclops supplies Night Shade, burns, Helping Hand and Pain Split. Specs Spectrier exploits burn-enhanced Hex and Mega Gengar closes with trapping pressure. Preserve speed reduction rather than adding a conflicting Trick Room mode.",
'TRAINER_GLACIA':"Alolan Ninetales opens Aurora Veil beside Specs Kyurem's Blizzard. Articuno supplies Tailwind and renews snow. Chien-Pao amplifies physical pressure, Walrein supplies Water coverage and Encore with Thick Fat durability, and Mega Baxcalibur remains the powerful closer. Snow, Veil and Tailwind have finite durations.",
'TRAINER_WALLACE':"Kyogre and Tapu Fini open rain pressure with Misty Terrain protection and Icy Wind. Ferrothorn answers Water and Fairy targets, Palkia supplies special coverage, and Milotic supports through Helping Hand and recovery. Huge Power Mega Starmie closes with rain-boosted physical Liquidation, Psycho Cut and Aqua Jet without removing the team's terrain.",
'TRAINER_WALLACE_DOUBLES_LEGENDS':"Kyogre and Therian Tornadus open rain and Tailwind. Arceus threatens Swords Dance/Extreme Speed, Calyrex supports with Helping Hand, Terapagos supplies selected-target Normal Tera Starstorm in its non-Stellar form, and Mega Mewtwo X closes with physical attacks. This is a one-time optional postgame talk exhibition; Diancite remains owned by the separate pickup.",
'TRAINER_STEVEN':"Skarmory supports Rayquaza with Tailwind, while Cradily supplies Storm Drain and recovery, Melmetal threatens Policy-enhanced physical damage and Dialga supplies special coverage. Mega Metagross is the signature planned finish. Dragon Ascent also makes Rayquaza Mega-eligible; one shared Mega activation is allocated by the common AI, favoring Metagross on equivalent lines rather than forbidding a necessary winning Rayquaza transformation."
}
partytext=(SRC/'src/data/trainers.party').read_text();native=(SRC/'src/data/trainers.h').read_text();master=(SRC/'data/emerald_champions/emerald_champions_master_battle_design.txt').read_text()
species=json.loads((BOOK/'inventory/species.json').read_text());formtext=(SRC/'src/data/pokemon/form_change_tables.h').read_text()
mega_by_item={m.group(2):m.group(1) for m in re.finditer(r'FORM_CHANGE_BATTLE_MEGA_EVOLUTION_ITEM,\s*(SPECIES_\w+),\s*ITEM_(\w+)',formtext)}
aliases=json.loads((BOOK/'inventory/species-aliases.json').read_text())
learn=json.loads((SRC/'data/emerald_champions/showdown_champions_learnsets.json').read_text())['learnsets']
def source_line(text,needle):
 pos=text.find(needle);return text.count('\n',0,pos)+1 if pos>=0 else None
def link(path,line,label):
 return f'[{label}](<{SRC/path}:{line}>)'
def table(mons):
 out=['| Slot | Pokémon | Item | Ability before form change | Nature | Points HP/Atk/Def/SpA/SpD/Spe | Cap offset | Moves |','|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---|']
 for i,m in enumerate(mons,1):out.append(f"| {i} | {m['species']} | {m['item']} | {m['ability']} | {m['nature']} | {m['points']} | {m['offset']:+d} | {' / '.join(m['moves'])} |")
 return '\n'.join(out)
def plain_plan(assessment):
 sentences=re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\s+',assessment)
 keep=[s for s in sentences if not re.search(r'\b(Preserve|Keep|Retain|Replace|This restores|The plan|the plan|the counterplay|the prose|the source|correct|stale|obsolete|already|nostalgia|ceremonial|propose)\b',s)]
 return ' '.join(keep) or assessment
records={}
for b in base:
 tid=b['trainer'];n=notes[tid];final=copy.deepcopy(b['mons']);delta=[]
 if tid in changes:
  c=changes[tid];before=copy.deepcopy(final[c['slot']]);final[c['slot']].update(c['updates']);delta=[{'slot':c['slot']+1,'before':before,'after':copy.deepcopy(final[c['slot']]),'reason':c['reason']}]
  # Check the precise proposed moves against the pinned authored legal input.
  key=re.sub('[^a-z0-9]','',final[c['slot']]['species'].lower());key={'zygarde50powerconstruct':'zygarde'}.get(key,key);assert key in learn,key
  for move in final[c['slot']]['moves']:assert move.replace('_','').lower() in learn[key],(tid,key,move)
  assert 'ABILITY_'+final[c['slot']]['ability'] in species['SPECIES_'+final[c['slot']]['species']]['abilities'],(tid,'ability')
 for m in final:
  points=list(map(int,m['points'].split('/')));assert len(points)==6 and max(points)<=32 and sum(points)<=66,(tid,points)
 assert len({m['item'] for m in final if m['item']!='NONE'})==len([m for m in final if m['item']!='NONE']),(tid,'item clause')
 sources={'teams':{'file':'data/emerald_champions/emerald_champions_battle_teams.txt','line':b['line']},'master':{'file':'data/emerald_champions/emerald_champions_master_battle_design.txt','line':source_line(master,'--- BRANCH '+tid+' ---')},'party':{'file':'src/data/trainers.party','line':source_line(partytext,'=== '+tid+' ===')},'native':{'file':'src/data/trainers.h','line':source_line(native,'[DIFFICULTY_NORMAL]['+tid+']')}}
 assert all(s['line'] for s in sources.values()),(tid,sources)
 finalplan=plans.get(tid,plain_plan(n['assessment']) if n['disposition']!='KEEP' else b['plan'])
 record={'encounter':b['encounter'],'trainer':tid,'class':b['cls'],'metadata':b['metadata'],'sources':sources,'baseline':{'plan':b['plan'],'counterplay':b['crack'],'ai_traits':b['ai'],'team':b['mons']},'disposition':n['disposition'],'assessment':n['assessment'],'lead_and_reserve_ai':n['ai'],'counterplay_review':n['counterplay'],'final_plan':finalplan,'final_team':final,'loadout_changes':delta,'final_ai_traits':b['ai'],'shared_ai_dependencies':['common expert decision standard','unbiased roll-aware damage','form-aware Mega and shared budget','live-cap Medium floor minus two',n['ai']],'acceptance':{'source':'Exact final loadout and source/master/native agreement; legal final species/items/abilities/moves and 66/32 Points.','battle':n['ai']+' Verify at least one favorable and one unfavorable board state for that decision using the actual effective levels and Points.','difficulty':'Native wins/losses and several viable player team approaches still require implementation-time battle evidence; no mathematical optimality or live playtest is claimed.'},'review_block':n['review_block'],'nostalgia':'See signature matrix in README.md.' if b['cls'] in ('leader','elite','rival','brain','admin') else None}
 records[tid]=record
(HERE/'review.json').write_text(json.dumps(records,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
encounters=sorted({b['encounter'] for b in base});groups=[encounters[i:i+20] for i in range(0,len(encounters),20)];index=[]
for num,ids in enumerate(groups,1):
 file=f'{num:02d}-E{ids[0]:04d}-E{ids[-1]:04d}.md';members=[b for b in base if b['encounter'] in ids];index.append((file,ids,members))
 text=[f'# Late battle review {num:02d} — E{ids[0]:04d}–E{ids[-1]:04d}',f'{len(ids)} retained encounter groups; {len(members)} independently reviewed trainer branches. See [volume contract](README.md). All tables reproduce the snapshot before proposals; no game file has been changed.','Points are **HP / Attack / Defense / Special Attack / Special Defense / Speed**. They are flat additions before Nature, with fixed perfect IVs. Offsets are authored inputs, **not guaranteed effective levels**. Apply the book\'s common runtime floor: Medium never falls below the current player cap minus two, including gyms. Ordinary standard teams have at least four; E0409 is one six-member opposing multi side owned three-plus-three.']
 for b in members:
  r=records[b['trainer']];tid=b['trainer'];s=r['sources'];text.extend([f"\n## E{b['encounter']:04d} — {tid}",f"**{r['disposition']}** · {b['cls']} · {b['metadata']['location']} · recorded cap {b['metadata']['strict_cap']} · {len(b['mons'])} members",'Source: '+ ' · '.join(link(x['file'],x['line'],k+':'+str(x['line'])) for k,x in s.items())+'.',f"**Current intent:** {b['plan']}",f"**Current counterplay prose:** {b['crack']}",f"**Current additional AI traits:** {', '.join(b['ai']) or 'none; the shared class profile still applies'}.",'### Baseline loadout',table(b['mons']),'### Individual assessment',r['assessment'],'**Lead, reserve and AI specification:** '+r['lead_and_reserve_ai'],'**Reviewed counterplay:** '+r['counterplay_review']])
  forms=[]
  for i,m in enumerate(r['final_team'],1):
   target=mega_by_item.get(m['item'])
   resolved=aliases.get('SPECIES_'+m['species'],'SPECIES_'+m['species'])
   exact=resolved+'_MEGA'
   if target and exact in species: target=exact
   if target and target in species:
    sp=species[target];src=sp.get('source');ref=link(src['file'],src['line'],target) if src else target
    forms.append(f"Slot {i}: {ref}; {' / '.join(t.replace('TYPE_','') for t in sp['types'])}; configured ability slots {' / '.join(a.replace('ABILITY_','') for a in sp['abilities'])}.")
  if forms:text.extend(['**Configured Mega forms:** '+' '.join(forms)+' Base-ability table entries above do not promise the same post-Mega ability.'])
  text.append('### Final specification')
  if r['loadout_changes']:
   text.extend([r['loadout_changes'][0]['reason'],'**Complete proposed final team:**',table(r['final_team'])])
  else:text.append('**Preserve the complete reproduced baseline loadout**, including species, item, ability slot, Nature, Points, authored offset, moves and slot order. No roster replacement is implied by a prose or shared-AI repair.')
  if r['disposition']!='KEEP':text.extend(['**Final authored plan:** '+r['final_plan'],'**Final authored counterplay:** '+r['counterplay_review']])
  else:text.append('Preserve the authored plan and trainer-specific loadout traits. The reviewed counterplay above is book guidance; it does not add a new gameplay restriction.')
  if tid=='TRAINER_WALLACE_DOUBLES_LEGENDS':text.append('**World dependency:** W-WALLACE-ROOT restores a talk-only Wallace object at (11,10), elevation 3, facing left in Diancie\'s room; game-clear gate, Yes/No invitation and existing one-time defeated state. Diancite remains with the existing pickup; remove the duplicate exhibition item grant. See the world volume for exact scripts and approach verification.')
  text.extend(['**Shared dependencies:** common expert AI, state-accurate ability/form/field evaluation, actual owner-scoped Mega budget, live player-cap floor and correct preparation/acquisition support. AI trait labels are subject to the central decision-policy specification, not permission to retain biased damage estimates.','**Acceptance after implementation:** '+r['acceptance']['source']+' '+r['acceptance']['battle']+' '+r['acceptance']['difficulty']])
 (HERE/file).write_text('\n\n'.join(text)+'\n')
summary={'scope':'encounter IDs greater than250','branches':len(base),'encounter_groups':len(encounters),'pokemon_slots':sum(len(b['mons']) for b in base),'dispositions':dict(collections.Counter(r['disposition'] for r in records.values())),'roster_revisions':list(changes),'native_battles_played':0,'changes_to_game':0,'coverage_complete':True,'entry_files':[x[0] for x in index]}
(BOOK/'review/late-battles.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2)+'\n')
readme=['# Late battle volume — complete branch-by-branch revision specification',f"This volume covers **{len(base)} branches, {len(encounters)} retained encounters and {summary['pokemon_slots']} Pokémon slots** from E0251 through E0513. Each branch received an individual source review of its actual loadout, lead/support interactions, reserve roles, competitive counterplay and governing AI dependencies. The 250 distinct assessments are manually authored in the review notes and rendered beside complete native loadouts; these are not automatic KEEP labels.",f"Disposition totals: {summary['dispositions']}. **Six branches have exact loadout revisions**; other REPAIR entries correct misleading authored explanations, restore the missing Wallace interaction or depend on shared state-aware AI work. Existing successful compositions remain the baseline.",'## Governing rules','The latest user decisions supersede the original opening exception: trainer competition has no singles, standard teams never have fewer than four, and every team receives the same expert tactical standard. Medium uses a runtime floor of current player cap minus two, including gyms. Three-member E0409 trainer contributions are one opposing six-member multi side. Preserve authored offsets and Points; the common runtime level rule determines effective levels. No IV-zero recommendation is valid under the configured fixed-IV31 Champions stat formula.',"Lilycove E0302 entries reproduce the six Hoenn authored templates. The early volume owns the regional resolver: the unchosen starter line from the player's two choices replaces only slot6, at the authored stage and +3 offset. The fixed Mega partner remains Metagross, Salamence or Tyranitar; the regional starter does not gain a second Mega entitlement.",
'Target the most coherent, capable and clever use of each roster. These source judgments do not establish mathematical global optimality or prove AI execution. Risky/Conservative may not hallucinate maximum/minimum damage rolls; the central AI specification owns probability-aware evaluation and can reinterpret historical trait labels.','## Read the catalog','| Chapter | Encounter groups | Branches |\n|---|---:|---:|']
for file,ids,members in index:readme.append(f'| [{file}]({file}) | {len(ids)} | {len(members)} |')
readme.extend(['## Exact loadout revisions','| Encounter | Change | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|', '| E0430 Ronald | Mega Raichu Y: Thunderbolt → Thunder | Exploit actual No Guard and Kingdra rain; retain all other data. |','| E0480 Quincy | Aura Break Zygarde50 → Power Construct50 | Enable Complete, the required prerequisite for the existing Zygardite Mega. |','| E0504 Colton | ordinary Floette → Eternal Flower Floette | Repair the exact base-species prerequisite for Floettite. |','| E0494 Phoebe | Shedinja → Eviolite Dusclops | Restore the signature Pokémon as burn, fixed-damage, Helping Hand and Pain Split support. |','| E0495 Glacia | Glastrier → Thick Fat Walrein | Restore the signature Pokémon with Water coverage, Encore and meaningful snow/Veil durability. |','| E0497 Wallace | Mega Starmie: special → Huge Power physical set | Give the real Mega ability a role and add physical rain pressure plus Aqua Jet. |','Each affected branch reproduces its entire final team. Legality of the changed Pokémon\'s moves and abilities was checked against the snapshot\'s pinned learnset input and configured species inventory. This does not replace materialization, build or live battle validation.','## Signature species decisions','| Principal trainer | Baseline identity and final decision |\n|---|---|','| Spenser | Crobat, Slaking and Lapras already identify the Palace Maven; preserve the six. |','| Winona | Altaria has a substantial Tailwind/Helping Hand role. Preserve Zapdos and other premium partners. |','| Maxie | Mightyena, Crobat and Camerupt remain in his hideout team; Crobat/Camerupt remain in the multi climax. Preserve. |','| Matt/Shelly | Keep their deliberate rain/faction identities and premium species; no invented single nostalgia species replaces their strategies. |','| Tate and Liza | Solrock/Lunatone lead a coherent low-Speed plan. Preserve. |','| Archie | Sharpedo is the actual Mega ace, with Tentacruel supporting rain. Correct obsolete Mega Eelektross prose. |','| Juan | Kingdra retains a strong Specs/Swift Swim role. Preserve. |','| Wally | Gallade preserves the defining Ralts-family bond in both late encounters; Roserade/Magnezone reinforce campaign familiarity. Preserve. |','| Sidney | Mega Absol Z is the signature closer. Preserve the legendary-heavy composition. |','| Phoebe | Restore Dusclops for Shedinja. Banette is a secondary nostalgic association considered but not added: two replacements would unnecessarily displace successful current roles. The restored primary signature is substantive. |','| Glacia | Restore Walrein for Glastrier. Glalie is a secondary association considered but not added: retain the established Ninetales/Kyurem engine, Articuno field support, Chien-Pao and Mega Baxcalibur. There is no arbitrary legendary cap. |','| Drake | Salamence already leads with Intimidate/Tailwind. Preserve. |','| Wallace | Milotic already supports the Champion team. Preserve it and optimize the separate Mega Starmie ace. The postgame legends exhibition is explicitly a different collection showcase. |','| Leaf | Kanto ensemble of Ninetales, Kangaskhan, Gengar, Tangrowth and Mewtwo supplies identity without inventing a mandatory starter. Preserve. |','| Steven | Skarmory, Cradily and Metagross form a strong iconic core. Preserve Rayquaza too; allocate its competing Mega eligibility through the shared decision policy, with Metagross the signature tie-break. |','| Cynthia | Roserade, Togekiss, Spiritomb, Lucario and Garchomp already create strong recognition. Preserve and correct Mega Garchomp Z typing. |','Glastrier\'s displaced campaign showcase is intentional. Its obtainability and Circuit eligibility remain global inventory responsibilities; no historical showcased-species count should force an unrelated swap. Shedinja remains elsewhere in the authored campaign.','## Cross-cutting findings and implementation order','1. Fix form-aware AI forecasting and owner-scoped Mega allocation before interpreting a rewritten loadout as a solution. Mega Starmie, Excadrill, Meganium, Meowstic, Victreebel, Glimmora, Clefable, Scolipede, Raichu X/Y, Floette and Garchomp Z demonstrate why base species assumptions are insufficient.','2. Implement the six precise loadout changes and the optional Wallace interaction restoration. Regenerate native parties from the existing authoring pipeline, preserving unrelated teams.','3. Replace erroneous plan/counterplay fields from REPAIR entries; dialogue must describe tactics or outcomes actually established, not assert that every player used one particular solution. Coordinate source script wording with the world volume.','4. Validate the shared decision dependencies against the actual revised teams: Choice-lock/Telepathy reserves, Palafin activation, Commander pairing, Surf-trigger engines, loss of speed/priority abilities on Mega, target immunities, weather renewal and probability-aware damage.','5. Conduct battle validation at actual Hard/Medium/Easy effective levels with fixed-IV31 flat Points. Restored iconic species must carry their specified roles in credible winning lines; documentation coverage alone is not proof of difficulty.','## Evidence and reproducibility','- [Machine-readable full review](review.json) contains every trainer ID, baseline and final roster, unique assessment, exact deltas, AI dependencies and acceptance criteria.','- [Volume coverage summary](../../review/late-battles.json) reconciles all 250 trainer IDs and 244 encounter groups.','- [Source-derived arithmetic and revision checks](benchmarks.md) records Points calculations and narrow legality checks.','- `render_volume.py`, `baseline.jsonl` and `notes-*.txt` are book-authoring helpers/data only. They do not replace game source or introduce new gameplay machinery.','No ROM, game source, native build artifact, save or installed game was modified. No battle was newly played during this documentation volume. Historical review records are context only; this volume\'s source snapshot and explicit future acceptance criteria define its evidence boundary.'])
(HERE/'README.md').write_text(re.sub(r'(?m)(^\|[^\n]*\n)\n(?=\|)',r'\1','\n\n'.join(readme))+'\n')
